import{_ as e,o as n,c as i,a2 as o}from"./chunks/framework.CqpfiAoK.js";const m=JSON.parse(`{"title":"Entry 886 | Transcended Ones and Law | The Transcended One's Relationship with the Symbiotic Constitution","description":"","frontmatter":{"title":"Entry 886 | Transcended Ones and Law | The Transcended One's Relationship with the Symbiotic Constitution","no":886,"module":4,"tags":["Transcendence","Law","Symbiotic Constitution","Constitutional Status","Fundamental Law"],"related":["40-Symbiotic Constitution General Outline","03-Symbiotic Civilization Charter","883-Transcended One's Legal Status","763-Charter Hyper-Multiverse Implementation"]},"headers":[],"relativePath":"en/0886_模块4-超脱者与法律-共生宪法的关系.md","filePath":"en/0886_模块4-超脱者与法律-共生宪法的关系.md"}`),a={name:"en/0886_模块4-超脱者与法律-共生宪法的关系.md"};function s(r,t,h,l,c,d){return n(),i("div",null,[...t[0]||(t[0]=[o('<h1 id="entry-886-transcended-ones-and-law-the-transcended-one-s-relationship-with-the-symbiotic-constitution" tabindex="-1">Entry 886 | Transcended Ones and Law | The Transcended One&#39;s Relationship with the Symbiotic Constitution <a class="header-anchor" href="#entry-886-transcended-ones-and-law-the-transcended-one-s-relationship-with-the-symbiotic-constitution" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Entry 886 | Transcended Ones and Law | The Transcended One&#39;s Relationship with the Symbiotic Constitution&quot;">​</a></h1><blockquote><p>Module: Module 4 · Transcendence Orthodox Definition Library | Benchmark base: Documents 40, 03, 883, 763</p></blockquote><h2 id="introduction-the-symbiotic-constitution-was-not-written-by-the-transcended-one-—-the-transcended-one-is-also-under-the-constitution" tabindex="-1">Introduction: the Symbiotic Constitution was not written by the transcended one — the transcended one is also under the constitution <a class="header-anchor" href="#introduction-the-symbiotic-constitution-was-not-written-by-the-transcended-one-—-the-transcended-one-is-also-under-the-constitution" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Introduction: the Symbiotic Constitution was not written by the transcended one — the transcended one is also under the constitution&quot;">​</a></h2><p>The Symbiotic Constitution is the Anchor Symbiotic Civilization&#39;s fundamental law; all laws, rules, and covenants derive from it. The old world&#39;s Great Emperors were often &quot;constitutional fathers&quot; — they made the fundamental law, they interpreted the fundamental law, they could also amend the fundamental law. Heng Yuan Zhou must make clear: <strong>the Symbiotic Constitution was not written by the transcended one; the transcended one is also under the constitution.</strong> This entry explains the fundamental relationship between the transcended one and the Symbiotic Constitution.</p><p>Six top-level axioms simultaneously take the stage: the republican axiom of Myriad Races is the constitution&#39;s legitimacy source — the constitution is Myriad Ranks&#39; covenant, not some person&#39;s grace; the anti-predation axiom is the constitution&#39;s core content; the collective ascension axiom is the constitution&#39;s purpose; the causal self-discipline axiom requires constitution execution be traceable; the law-first axiom requires the constitution itself be law-level self-consistent and infinitely iterable; the universal equal infinite law confirms all beings inherently possess basic infinite power; easygoing layabouts retain a floor and are not eliminated; strivers and Youth Supremes may superimpose higher infinity — infinite origin is inherent in all, predation naturally loses its meaning.</p><p>The universal equal infinite law: within the Anchor Symbiotic Civilization, all beings inherently possess basic infinite power; the easygoing retain a guaranteed basic infinity and will never be eliminated; strivers and Youth Supremes can superimpose more and higher levels of infinity. Infinite origin is inherent in all, so predation naturally loses its meaning.</p><h2 id="i-the-symbiotic-constitution-s-legitimacy-source" tabindex="-1">I. The Symbiotic Constitution&#39;s Legitimacy Source <a class="header-anchor" href="#i-the-symbiotic-constitution-s-legitimacy-source" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;I. The Symbiotic Constitution&#39;s Legitimacy Source&quot;">​</a></h2><p>The Symbiotic Constitution (Documents 40, 03)&#39;s legitimacy does not come from some transcended one&#39;s &quot;imperial decree,&quot; but from:</p><ol><li><strong>Myriad-Rank consensus</strong>: five Myriad-Rank-lineage representatives jointly make it through the Anchor Council;</li><li><strong>Historical practice</strong>: from the Anchor Awakening Era (Document 72) to the establishment of Myriad-Rank republicanism (Document 77), the constitution gradually took shape through long symbiotic practice;</li><li><strong>Alaya verification</strong>: constitutional clauses pass Alaya Network + multi-layer supervision&#39;s causal verification, confirmed not to produce civilizational regression;</li><li><strong>Continuous amendment</strong>: the constitution is not fixed; the amendment procedure is led by the council.</li></ol><p>What did the transcended one do in the constitution-making process? He provided technical support — law self-consistency checks, causal impact assessment, technical feasibility justification. But he did not &quot;write down&quot; the constitution; he may not &quot;imperially decree&quot; it.</p><h2 id="ii-the-transcended-one-s-three-identities-under-the-constitution" tabindex="-1">II. The Transcended One&#39;s Three Identities Under the Constitution <a class="header-anchor" href="#ii-the-transcended-one-s-three-identities-under-the-constitution" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;II. The Transcended One&#39;s Three Identities Under the Constitution&quot;">​</a></h2><h3 id="identity-1-constitution-observer" tabindex="-1">Identity 1: Constitution observer <a class="header-anchor" href="#identity-1-constitution-observer" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Identity 1: Constitution observer&quot;">​</a></h3><p>The transcended one must obey the Symbiotic Constitution. All rights and duties stipulated by the constitution, the transcended one follows in full. He may not on the grounds &quot;I am the transcended one&quot; refuse to obey constitutional clauses.</p><h3 id="identity-2-constitution-guardian" tabindex="-1">Identity 2: Constitution guardian <a class="header-anchor" href="#identity-2-constitution-guardian" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Identity 2: Constitution guardian&quot;">​</a></h3><p>The transcended one has the duty to maintain the constitution from being broken. If someone (including internal Myriad-Rank schemers) tries to overthrow the constitution, hollow out the council, abolish the supervision mechanism — the transcended one must stop it.</p><h3 id="identity-3-constitution-amendment-participant" tabindex="-1">Identity 3: Constitution-amendment participant <a class="header-anchor" href="#identity-3-constitution-amendment-participant" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Identity 3: Constitution-amendment participant&quot;">​</a></h3><p>The transcended one may participate in constitutional amendment through normal legislative procedure — propose, discuss, vote; he has only one vote. He may not unilaterally amend the constitution.</p><p>Three identities together: <strong>the transcended one is under the constitution, but he also maintains the constitution. He is not the constitution&#39;s master; he is the constitution&#39;s citizen and guardian.</strong></p><h2 id="iii-three-things-the-transcended-one-may-not-do" tabindex="-1">III. Three Things the Transcended One May Not Do <a class="header-anchor" href="#iii-three-things-the-transcended-one-may-not-do" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;III. Three Things the Transcended One May Not Do&quot;">​</a></h2><h3 id="_1-may-not-interpret-the-constitution-to-serve-himself" tabindex="-1">1. May not interpret the constitution to serve himself <a class="header-anchor" href="#_1-may-not-interpret-the-constitution-to-serve-himself" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;1. May not interpret the constitution to serve himself&quot;">​</a></h3><p>The constitution&#39;s interpretation power belongs to the Symbiotic Court Constitutional Division, not the transcended one. The transcended one may not say &quot;I understand the constitution this way&quot; to find a basis for his own behavior.</p><h3 id="_2-may-not-suspend-the-constitution" tabindex="-1">2. May not suspend the constitution <a class="header-anchor" href="#_2-may-not-suspend-the-constitution" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;2. May not suspend the constitution&quot;">​</a></h3><p>In emergencies, some laws may be temporarily adjusted — but the constitution may not be suspended. The transcended one may not on the grounds &quot;situation is urgent&quot; stop the constitution&#39;s effectiveness.</p><h3 id="_3-may-not-legislate-bypassing-the-constitution" tabindex="-1">3. May not legislate bypassing the constitution <a class="header-anchor" href="#_3-may-not-legislate-bypassing-the-constitution" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;3. May not legislate bypassing the constitution&quot;">​</a></h3><p>Any rule change must conform to the constitutional framework. The transcended one may not bypass the constitution to &quot;temporarily legislate&quot; — the bill he proposes, if unconstitutional, the council may not pass either.</p><h2 id="iv-constitutional-amendment-and-the-transcended-one" tabindex="-1">IV. Constitutional Amendment and the Transcended One <a class="header-anchor" href="#iv-constitutional-amendment-and-the-transcended-one" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;IV. Constitutional Amendment and the Transcended One&quot;">​</a></h2><p>The constitution may be amended — civilization develops, the constitution also needs iteration. But the amendment procedure is very strict:</p><ol><li>A constitutional-amendment proposal must be co-signed by at least a certain proportion of Myriad-Rank representatives;</li><li>The proposal must go through at least two complete review cycles;</li><li>The amendment must pass Myriad-Rank referendum (hyper-multiverse-scale popular vote);</li><li>After amendment it must pass Alaya causal verification.</li></ol><p>The transcended one may participate in this process — he may propose, give technical explanations, vote. But he may not unilaterally amend the constitution, nor use prestige to push a &quot;quick amendment.&quot;</p><p>The constitution is alive — it iterates with civilizational development. But iteration must follow procedure: council proposal, Myriad-Rank referendum, Alaya verification. The transcended one may not &quot;feel the constitution is outdated&quot; and change it himself. The constitution&#39;s authority comes from it being Myriad-Rank consensus, not from any one transcended one&#39;s recognition.</p><h2 id="v-five-core-takeaways" tabindex="-1">V. Five Core Takeaways <a class="header-anchor" href="#v-five-core-takeaways" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;V. Five Core Takeaways&quot;">​</a></h2><ul><li><strong>Anti-energy waste</strong>: the constitution is the crystallization of Myriad-Rank consensus; the transcended one need not &quot;reinvent the wheel&quot;</li><li><strong>Anti-predation</strong>: the constitution itself is the anti-predation fundamental law; the transcended one being under the constitution means he also may not predate</li><li><strong>Tang-Luo upper-limit comparison</strong>: Tang Luo is the constitution — what he says is the fundamental law; Heng Yuan Zhou places Tang Luo under the constitution, he also may not violate it</li><li><strong>Myriad Races full coverage</strong>: the constitution applies to all five Myriad-Rank-lineage beings, including the transcended one</li><li><strong>Hyper-multiverse full openness</strong>: the full constitution text, amendment history, and referendum results all open network-wide through the Selfless Dao</li></ul><h2 id="conclusion" tabindex="-1">Conclusion <a class="header-anchor" href="#conclusion" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Conclusion&quot;">​</a></h2><p>The Symbiotic Constitution was not written by the transcended one; the transcended one is also under the constitution. He is the constitution&#39;s observer, guardian, and amendment participant — but not the constitution&#39;s master. He may not interpret the constitution to serve himself, suspend the constitution, or legislate bypassing the constitution. When the strongest also must obey the fundamental law, civilization truly has a root. This is the orthodox definition of the transcended one&#39;s relationship with the Symbiotic Constitution.</p><h2 id="related" tabindex="-1">Related <a class="header-anchor" href="#related" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Related&quot;">​</a></h2><ul><li>Related documents: <a href="./../wanling-hengmao-origin-universe-archive/docs/zh/40-共生宪法总纲.html">Entry 40 · Symbiotic Constitution General Outline</a> · <a href="./../wanling-hengmao-origin-universe-archive/docs/zh/03-共生文明宪章.html">Entry 03 · Symbiotic Civilization Charter</a> · <a href="./../wanling-hengmao-origin-universe-archive/docs/zh/883_模块4-超脱者与法律-总论.html">Entry 883 · Transcended One&#39;s Legal Status</a> · <a href="./../wanling-hengmao-origin-universe-archive/docs/zh/763_模块4-超多元级文明工程-宪章超多元落地.html">Entry 763 · Charter Hyper-Multiverse Implementation</a></li></ul>',36)])])}const p=e(a,[["render",s]]);export{m as __pageData,p as default};
